In Ladybird, an opaque system selection color is made translucent, so
that it looks like itself over white, only in a light color scheme. A
dark scheme keeps the color as it is, at alpha 204. Blink’s Color::
BlendWithWhite() and WebKit’s blendWithWhite() compute the same
translucent color for a light scheme. On macOS in a dark scheme, Blink’s
LayoutTheme::ActiveSelectionBackgroundColor() keeps the system color’s
RGB at alpha 204, and WebKit gives an opaque one alpha 0.8, as Ladybird
now does. Gecko applies no general transparency on Linux, and on macOS
leaves the selection color of a dark appearance unchanged.
